  "solution": {
    "text": "The length of carbon-carbon single bond is always greater than that of the carbon-carbon double bond.\r\nIn III, positive charge is not in conjugation of double bond, so the bond does not acquire a double bond character. However, chances of acquiring double bond character fof the indicated bond) is much more in I than that in case of II.\r\nThus, the correct order of decreasing bond length is\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2014_che_a14.png\">",
